@@ -1,27 +1,10 @@
-# Veðurspá historical comparison build
+# Veðurspá 1.6
 
-This source package builds versionCode 4 / versionName 1.3.
-
-Automatic Android history collection:
-- 24 hours after a complete successful collection.
-- If any forecast or actual-observation collection is failed/partial, retry in 1 hour.
-- Continue hourly until complete, then return to the 24-hour schedule.
-- Wi-Fi-only and retention settings are synchronized from the history UI.
-- The schedule is restored after reboot, app replacement, or app launch.
-
-Historical comparison:
-- Two always-accessible sliders choose the saved forecast run and the valid forecast time.
-- Pinned Spá / Raun / Bera saman controls avoid scrolling to switch views.
-- Compare mode supports stacked forecast-over-actual maps and a draggable reveal divider.
-- The divider button cycles forecast / 50-50 / actual views.
-- Actual precipitation first uses the long-term Veðurstofa Iceland RTR radar archive nearest the selected valid time (within 15 minutes). The radar precipitation pixels are isolated, recoloured to the forecast precipitation scale, and calibrated onto the same Iceland framing as the archived forecast map.
-- If an archived radar frame is unavailable, precipitation falls back to a continuous measured field interpolated from Veðurstofa station totals on the same forecast-map reference, with station values available as detail points.
-- Temperature, wind and cloud use measured station observations projected onto that same forecast-map reference, so the geography remains consistent between forecast and actual views.
-- Native background collections archive the observation page and station metadata so station-based actual data remains available after it drops off the live observation page.
-- Viewed radar images are cached locally by the history UI; the long-term public radar archive is used so old comparisons do not depend on the short-lived current-radar image directory.
-
-Version 1.3 changes:
-- Replaced the sparse precipitation-dot comparison with archived RTR radar as the primary actual precipitation layer.
-- Calibrated and recoloured radar precipitation onto the same forecast-map framing for useful stacked and draggable comparisons.
-- Kept station interpolation as a fallback rather than the main rain comparison.
-- Reduced empty map-card space and kept comparison controls pinned on screen.
+Changes:
+- Fixed Northern Lights cloud scoring: numeric Staðaspá cloud cover is primary; corrected green/white map sampling is fallback.
+- Best-in-night now evaluates real cloud forecasts for dark hours instead of synthetic estimates.
+- Staðaspá includes an interactive Iceland map/time slider and Besta veðrið clear+warm finder.
+- Warning screen includes an Iceland warning map with a time slider.
+- Top navigation and touch targets enlarged.
+- Test fixtures/tools are isolated behind hidden Developer Mode (tap version 7 times to enable).
+- Warning notifications remain free.
